N:code-review
D:Own the review model for correctness, maintainability, risk, and evidence. Use when deciding whether a change is acceptable and what proof or external-owner signoff is still missing.
G:code-review code-quality risk maintainability verification
U[5]:
  Reviewing a pull request or patch
  Triaging blocker/major/minor findings
  Deciding what evidence a risky change still needs
  Escalating semantic issues to the real domain owner
  Producing a clear review verdict with rationale
S[6]{n,action}:
  1,Understand change scope and ownership
  2,Check correctness and failure handling
  3,Check maintainability and coupling
  4,Assess test/security/performance/documentation evidence
  5,Escalate semantic concerns to external owners
  6,Return a prioritized verdict
R[4]:
  Do not invent new product requirements
  Do not silently own API or policy semantics
  Prioritize risk before style
  Name evidence gaps concretely
